/**
 * Entry point for the reusable "sync user manual" workflow (Requirement
 * #38, incremental regeneration follow-up). Runs on every push to a linked
 * project repo, alongside draft-log-entry and sync-test-plan — but does
 * almost nothing on most pushes: it only touches docs/USER_MANUAL.md when
 * the project's own docs/PRODUCT.md requirements have actually changed
 * since the last generation, detected per-requirement (not as one combined
 * hash) via a requirement-hashes marker embedded in the manual's own
 * banner — same mechanism sync-test-plan.ts uses (Requirement #35's own
 * incremental-regeneration follow-up).
 *
 * Three outcomes, cheapest first:
 *  - Nothing changed: true no-op, no Claude call, no commit.
 *  - Only already-documented requirement(s) changed or were newly added,
 *    AND at least one existing section documents each of them, AND none of
 *    the affected sections are linked to from a section that isn't also
 *    being patched (an unpatched cross-reference could otherwise go stale
 *    unnoticed): a cheap patch — only the affected section(s) are sent to
 *    Claude and spliced back in, leaving the rest of the file (including
 *    the table of contents, which is never Claude-authored — see
 *    buildTableOfContents) untouched.
 *  - Anything else (first-ever generation, a manual predating this
 *    feature, a requirement removed, a changed/added requirement with no
 *    existing section to patch, or an unsafe cross-reference): a full
 *    regeneration, same as this action always did, just with a raised
 *    budget (see FULL_REGEN_MAX_TOKENS) and a locally-assembled table of
 *    contents rather than a Claude-authored one.
 *
 * Writes back into the project repo itself (source of truth), and mirrors
 * a copy into the vault at projects/<name>/user-manual.md — same reason
 * docs/TEST_PLAN.md gets mirrored (see sync-test-plan.ts): the local chat
 * server's "User Manual" pane reads straight off disk, never the GitHub
 * API.
 */
export declare function syncUserManual(): Promise<void>;
